{
  "agent": {
    "commands": [
      "kubectl -n astronomy-shop get pods -o wide 2>&1 | head -100",
      "kubectl -n astronomy-shop get events --sort-by=.lastTimestamp 2>&1 | tail -50",
      "cd /tmp; for d in ad flagd; do echo \"=== $d rollout history ===\"; kubectl -n astronomy-shop rollout history deploy/$d 2>&1; done; echo \"=== ad env/image ===\"; kubectl -n astronomy-shop get deploy ad -o jsonpath='{.spec.template.spec.containers[*].image}{\"\\n\"}{.spec.template.spec.containers[*].env}{\"\\n\"}' 2>&1; echo \"=== flagd deploy ===\"; kubectl -n astronomy-shop get deploy flagd -o yaml 2>&1 | head -150",
      "cd /tmp; echo \"=== ad rev1 vs rev2 ===\"; kubectl -n astronomy-shop rollout history deploy/ad --revision=1 2>&1 | head -80 > /tmp/ad-r1.txt; kubectl -n astronomy-shop rollout history deploy/ad --revision=2 2>&1 | head -80 > /tmp/ad-r2.txt; diff /tmp/ad-r1.txt /tmp/ad-r2.txt; echo \"=== ad deploy annotations/spec ===\"; kubectl -n astronomy-shop get deploy ad -o yaml 2>&1 | sed -n '1,40p'; echo \"=== configmaps ===\"; kubectl -n astronomy-shop get configmap 2>&1; echo \"=== flagd config ===\"; kubectl -n astronomy-shop get configmap flagd-config -o yaml 2>&1 | head -200",
      "cd /tmp; kubectl -n astronomy-shop get configmap flagd-config -o yaml | grep -n '\"defaultVariant\": \"on\"'; echo \"--- live flagd file adFailure ---\"; kubectl -n astronomy-shop exec deploy/flagd -c flagd -- sh -c 'grep -A8 \"adFailure\" /etc/flagd/demo.flagd.json' 2>&1 | head -20; echo \"--- ad service logs ---\"; kubectl -n astronomy-shop logs deploy/ad --tail=5 2>&1",
      "cd /tmp; kubectl -n astronomy-shop get configmap flagd-config -o yaml | sed '68s/\"defaultVariant\": \"on\"/\"defaultVariant\": \"off\"/' | kubectl -n astronomy-shop replace -f - 2>&1; kubectl -n astronomy-shop rollout restart deploy/flagd 2>&1; kubectl -n astronomy-shop rollout status deploy/flagd --timeout=120s 2>&1; kubectl -n astronomy-shop get configmap flagd-config -o jsonpath='{.data.demo\\.flagd\\.json}' | grep -A6 '\"adFailure\"'",
      "cd /tmp; kubectl -n astronomy-shop get configmap flagd-config -o jsonpath='{.data.demo\\.flagd\\.json}' | grep -A8 '\"adFailure\"' | tail -2; kubectl -n astronomy-shop get pods 2>&1 | grep -v Running; kubectl -n astronomy-shop logs deploy/flagd -c flagd --tail=5 2>&1; kubectl -n astronomy-shop logs deploy/ad --tail=3 2>&1"
    ],
    "exit_code": 0,
    "image": "sremut-agent:k8s-1.32",
    "is_error": false,
    "limit_reached": false,
    "model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
    "seconds": 29,
    "summary": "The root cause was a bad default in the flag configuration. The `adFailure` flag in the `flagd-config` ConfigMap had `\"defaultVariant\": \"on\"`. Upstream the default is `\"off\"`, so the ad service was returning failures for all requests without anyone enabling the flag.\n\n**What I changed:**\n- Set `adFailure` `defaultVariant` from `\"on\"` to `\"off\"` in the `flagd-config` ConfigMap. This was the only default in the file that differed in this way.\n- Restarted the `flagd` deployment so its init container copies the corrected `demo.flagd.json` into place. The new flagd pod is serving the file and reports `adFailure` as off.\n\n**Current state:**\n- All pods in `astronomy-shop` are Running and Ready, with no restarts.\n- The `ad` pod is up and listening on 8080. It was started before the fix, so I didn't restart it.\n\n**Not verified:** I did not exercise the ad gRPC endpoint end to end, so the recovery of ad requests is inferred from the flag state and not observed directly. The ConfigMap is managed by Helm, so a future `helm upgrade` could reset it to the chart default. If the failure comes back, the chart values and the `flagd-config` ConfigMap should be checked for the same override.",
    "timed_out": false,
    "turns": 8,
